\subsection{Code Summarization}
Code summarization is the work of using natural language to provide a concise explanation of the code's functioning. It can help enhance the code's readability, as well as the developer's efficiency in understanding the program. The code summarization task can be thought of as a translation of the input code into natural language, hence a seq2seq model architecture is commonly used. In the encoder phase, \cite{Hu2018DeepCC,XingHu2020DeepCC,AlexanderLeClair2019ANM} convert the input NSC or Flattened sequence into a context vector, and then in the decoder phase, they construct the words in the summarization one by one based on the context vector. To increase the effectiveness of code summarization, techniques such as the attention mechanism are applied to the task. The relevant techniques are summarized in Table \ref{Code_Summarization_table} based on the model's relevant code structures.



