\cos(2\theta_0)\delta Q_{xx}+ \sin(2\theta_0) \delta Q_{xy} = \frac{\alpha \mu}{2c S_0^2}\left[\cos(2\theta_0)\delta\varepsilon_{xx}+\sin(2\theta_0)\delta\varepsilon_{xy}\right].
\end{equation}
There are two reference nematic orientations $\theta_0$ for which these perturbations decouple: 
