where an integration of the model output $J_\mathrm{p}(P,K_0)$ is computed within each rigidity bin $\Delta P_j$, while $\hat{J}_\mathrm{p,\, j}$ is the mean value of the data. Factors $\sigma_j$ account for the experimental uncertainties in the measured fluxes.
The results demonstrate that, despite the approximations, the model effectively reconstructs the cosmic ray flux during any phase of solar activity.
