The bottom row displays the smooth cross-correlation function $\vec{f}$ during the negative and positive polarity phases, alongside the original $K_0(t)$ values for reference, plotted against the $S(t\mathord{-}\tau)$ proxy. These plots demonstrate how the long-term evolution of the model's modulation parameter is effectively captured by the derived cross-correlation functions.}
