\subsection{The Sobol' and SSRCA Methods identify similar sensitive parameters}

We compared the sensitivity analysis results that result from using the SSRCA and Sobol' Methods. For the Sobol' Method, we computed the averaged total effect effect indices, $\bar{S}_{T_q}$ from Equation \eqref{eq:mean_total_effect_index}, when varying all 10 parameters to generate the Saltelli Dataset. Both methods yield similar sensitivity analysis results. The $\bar{S}_{T_q}$ values are highest (indicative of high sensitivity) for the $c_a$ and $c_d$ parameters, followed by moderate $\bar{S}_{T_q}$ values for the $\eta_1$ and $\eta_3$ parameters; all other parameters have small $\bar{S}_{T_q}$ values (indicative of low sensitivity). The SSRCA method classifies these same four parameters as sensitive and all others as insensitive.

