\section{Gaussian Overbound of Multipath and Code Noise}\label{app:cnmp_bound}
The Gaussian overbound for multipath and code noise error for code IF combination is given by
\begin{equation}
    \sigma^i_{\varrho, user, j , AB} = \sigma^i_{\varrho, user, j} \sqrt{\frac{\gamma^2 +1}{(\gamma-1)^2}}\,,
\end{equation}
where $\gamma = f_A^2/f_B^2$ is the ratio of squares of two frequencies, and
\begin{equation}
    \sigma^i_{\varrho, user, j} = \sqrt{(\sigma^i_{\varrho, noise, j})^2+(\sigma^i_{\varrho, multipath, j})^2} \,.
\end{equation}
The code noise bound $\sigma^i_{\varrho, noise, j}$ and multipath bound $\sigma^i_{\varrho, multipath, j}$ after carrier smoothing suggested by WGC are provided by\par
