To improve estimation, we introduce a heuristic based on the condition: 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:heuristic}
    \frac{f_n(t) - f_n(t-\delta t)}{\delta t} > \epsilon_{\delta}
\end{equation}
%$\frac{f_n(t) - f_n(t-\delta t)}{\delta t} > \epsilon_{\delta}$
as a filter to temporarily halt the estimation over a time interval of $\Delta t$ enables the estimation to take place in regions where the dynamics are less adverse. The estimator is run with the added heuristic on the same data as in Fig. \ref{fig:no_heuristics}, and the updated results are shown in Fig. \ref{fig:dfn_heuristics}. Here it can be seen that the estimated $\mu_c$ values are higher and more stable, it can also be seen that both fingers of the gripper estimate similar $\mu_c$ values.
