The estimator is tested under planar motion, where both rotational and linear motion occur at the same time. This is achieved by letting the gripper hold the object vertically and then rotating the gripper around the object, see Fig. \ref{fig:gripper_hinge}. The results for each material can be seen in Table \ref{tab:est}, and shows that the estimation outcome is similar to the linear case. It is noteworthy that, as the normal force changes less during the planar experiment, the heuristic has less effect on the estimation, which can be observed in Table \ref{tab:est}. 

