\subsection*{Existence of required polynomials}
\subsubsection*{Dimensions smaller than 14}
In this subsection, we prove the following result.
\begin{proposition}
There exist a non-$(3)$-cyclic isogeny class of $g$-dimensional abelian varieties defined over $\mathbb{F}_q$ for any $g$ such that $2\leq g\leq 13$, except in the cases $(g,\mathbb{F}_q) \in \{(2,\mathbb{F}_2), (2,\mathbb{F}_3), (3,\mathbb{F}_2)\}$. In the exceptional cases, the non-$(\ell)$-cyclic classes are only for $\ell=2$, and the Weil polynomials of the complete list of non-cyclic isogeny classes are given in Table \ref{tab:exceptions}.
\end{proposition}

