\end{equation}
and the localized default indicator process $H^n_{\cdot} \coloneqq \mathbbm{1}_{\tau^n \leq \cdot}$. To the define the localized equity process, by enlarging the probability space, assume there is a $d$-dimensional Brownian motion $\wh{W}$ independent of $U,W$ and $B$. The filtration  $\filtg^n$ is the $\prob$ augmented version of $\filt^{W, B,\wh{W}} \vee \filt^{H^n}$. The equity market in this local investment problem has the following price dynamics:
\begin{equation*}
